# `core.autocrlf=true` is set system-wide on Windows installs of Git, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. Vite's transform rejects CRLF in some .mjs
# files at import time with `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`, while
# `node --check` and bare `node` accept the same file — so a whole test suite
# can silently stop running while the summary still reads green. That happened
# in claude-grok-delegate (two suites, unnoticed). `text=auto eol=lf` overrides
# autocrlf for this repo so a fresh clone cannot reintroduce it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
